# madcide keybinding profile: VS Code's keys (plan §41.11a step 3e) — its
# published default keymap, the Linux and macOS sheets (code.visualstudio.
# com/shortcuts/keyboard-shortcuts-linux.pdf and -macos.pdf) and the
# default-keybindings page, read 2026-10-01, onto the one action
# vocabulary. `primary` is Ctrl, or Cmd on macOS: VS Code's two sheets
# differ by that swap for most commands; a `ctrl+` line is Ctrl on both
# (Go to Line, Ctrl+Tab, the terminal). Ctrl+K opens chords, as in VS
# Code. Shift with any motion selects (the engine's rule). Until the
# debugger (Phase 7) F5 and Ctrl+F5 both run.
#
# Where macOS uses a different KEY, not just Cmd, the Linux key is bound
# on every platform (a profile has one key per binding): the file's ends
# (Ctrl+Home / Ctrl+End; macOS ⌘↑ / ⌘↓), the word motions (Ctrl+arrows;
# macOS ⌥←/⌥→), Find next (F3; macOS ⌘G) and Redo (Ctrl+Y; macOS ⇧⌘Z).
#
# VS Code's keys whose command madcide does not have yet are listed, not
# invented: New File (Ctrl+N), Close (Ctrl+W), Close All (Ctrl+K Ctrl+W),
# Save All (Ctrl+K S; macOS ⌥⌘S), Replace (Ctrl+H), Find previous
# (Shift+F3), Toggle line comment (Ctrl+/), Trigger suggestion
# (Ctrl+Space), Move line (Alt+Up / Alt+Down), Insert line below / above
# (Ctrl+Enter, Ctrl+Shift+Enter), Go to Definition (F12), next / previous
# problem (F8 / Shift+F8), the Command Palette (Ctrl+Shift+P, F1), the
# debugger's steps and breakpoints (F9, F10, F11, Shift+F11), zoom
# (Ctrl+= / Ctrl+-) and full screen (F11).
@title VS Code

# File management
primary+o editfile
primary+s save
primary+shift+s saveas
ctrl+tab bufsel
# Basic editing
primary+z undo
primary+y redo
primary+x cut
primary+c copy
primary+v paste
primary+a selectall
primary+shift+k delline
ctrl+home top
ctrl+end bottom
ctrl+left wordleft
ctrl+right wordright
ctrl+del delword
# Search and navigation
primary+f find
f3 findnext
ctrl+g gotoline
primary+p project
primary+shift+e project
primary+shift+o outline
primary+shift+m problems
primary+shift+u output
# Editor management: split, and focus the previous / next group
primary+\ splitw
primary+k primary+left prevw
primary+k primary+right nextw
# Run (F5 / Ctrl+F5) and stop (Shift+F5); the integrated terminal
f5 replrun
ctrl+f5 replrun
shift+f5 replstop
ctrl+` terminal
# Quit: VS Code's on Linux (Ctrl+Q) and macOS (⌘Q), off its sheets.
primary+q quit
# The project window's keys (@project scope — profile data; the baked
# defaults add esc/backspace).
@project ins projadd
@project del projdel
@project enter projopen
